# Hotfix propagation chain, most-stable FIRST. THIS FILE DOES NOTHING.
# Copy it to .claude/hotfix-chain in a repo to arm .claude/hooks/hotfix.sh there.
#
# The hook merges each branch into the next one down, but only commits whose
# subject starts with `hotfix:` / `hotfix(scope):` / `hotfix!:`. A fix made on
# release reaches every branch below it without a cherry-pick, and nothing
# else moves. Local only: it never fetches, pushes or deploys.
#
# DECIDE FIRST: a branch per environment is one deployment model; promoting one
# immutable artifact dev → uat → prod from a single main branch is another.
# If your CI promotes artifacts, do NOT arm this — the two would disagree about
# what is deployed where.

release
uat
main
